\ ==== matrix poly ====

\ one-arg form: cols computed from array length and rows
[ 1 2 3 4 5 6 ] 2 matrix .
[ 1 2 3 4 5 6 ] 3 matrix .
[ 1 2 3 4 5 6 ] 6 matrix .
[ 1 2 3 4 5 6 ] 1 matrix .

\ one-arg with a single-element array
[ 42 ] 1 matrix .

\ two-arg form still works (unchanged behavior)
[ 1 2 3 4 5 6 ] 2 3 matrix .
[ 1 2 3 4 ] 2 2 matrix .

\ same matrix from one-arg and two-arg forms
[ 10 20 30 40 ] 2 matrix .
[ 10 20 30 40 ] 2 2 matrix .

\ composes with other matrix words
[ 1 2 3 4 ] 2 matrix transpose .
[ 1 2 3 4 5 6 ] 2 matrix dim . .

\ failures
[ 1 2 3 4 5 ] 2 matrix
[ 1 2 3 ] 0 matrix
[ 1 2 3 ] -1 matrix
"x" 2 matrix
5 matrix
matrix

clear

\ ==== matrix range ====

\ matrix-range: build a 1xN matrix from start/end/step.

\ Basic ascending sequence
1.0 5.0 1.0 matrix-range .

\ Ascending with non-unit step
0.0 10.0 2.5 matrix-range .

\ Descending sequence
10.0 0.0 -2.0 matrix-range .

\ Single-element matrix (start = end)
3.0 3.0 1.0 matrix-range .

\ End not on an exact step boundary — last element is [< end
0.0 10.0 3.0 matrix-range .

\ Step zero rejected
1.0 5.0 0.0 matrix-range

\ Step sign / direction mismatch rejected
1.0 5.0 -1.0 matrix-range

\ Element count overflows int (M3) — must error, not cast a huge double to int
0.0 1e18 0.001 matrix-range

\ Non-finite bounds rejected: inf/inf would make (end-start)/step a NaN that
\ slips past the count guard and casts NaN to int
inf inf 1.0 matrix-range
0.0 inf 1.0 matrix-range

clear
